  "articleBody": "Upgrading a garage interior into a clean, functional workshop, gym, or organized storage space requires thoughtful planning before ordering cabinets or hanging drywall. Everyday utility spaces face temperature swings, vehicle fumes, and heavy wear that typical interior rooms never encounter.\n\nOverview and Process Breakdown:\nA quality garage renovation starts with an envelope inspection. Checking for water leaks, concrete settling cracks, and drafty garage doors ensures you do not conceal existing damage. Next comes utility planning, identifying outlet locations for tools, lighting needs, and ventilation. Finally, proper moisture-resistant insulation, drywall finishing, paint, and durable floor systems complete the transformation.\n\nWhat to Prepare Before You Start:\n- Map out dedicated equipment and heavy storage zones to ensure wall framing has proper blocking.\n- Evaluate your electrical panel capacity for additional circuits and high-output lighting.\n- Choose durable wall finishes that resist scuffs and handle Colorado humidity shifts.\n- Never extend central house furnace ducts into a working garage, as this creates air-quality and code hazards.\n\nHH Remodeling LLC brings years of hands-on finish carpentry, drywall, and remodeling craftsmanship to every project. Contact Abraham Becerra at 303-505-0866 to get started on your garage upgrade.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}